  "alt": "The same extraction prompt sent through three mechanisms. JSON mode guarantees only syntactically valid JSON, so a field can come back with the wrong type. Function calling lets the model decide whether to call a tool at all. Structured outputs constrain decoding to the schema, so every response matches it.",
  "caption": "JSON mode guarantees valid JSON, not your schema. Structured outputs enforce the schema at the token level.",
